        <abstract>
          <title>Abstract</title>
          <sec>
            <title>Background</title>
            <p>Biomedical literature mining requires efficient XML parsing techniques to extract structured information from PubMed and PMC databases.</p>
          </sec>
          <sec>
            <title>Methods</title>
            <p>We developed a comprehensive Java-based XML parser using StAX technology for memory-efficient processing of large-scale biomedical literature datasets.</p>
          </sec>
          <sec>
            <title>Results</title>
            <p>Our parser achieved 95% accuracy in extracting metadata and demonstrated significant performance improvements over existing solutions.</p>
          </sec>
          <sec>
            <title>Conclusion</title>
            <p>The proposed XML parsing framework provides a robust foundation for biomedical text mining applications.</p>
          </sec>
        </abstract>
